-- title:
--   Descent of a twisted Γ-invariant family to the Fr²-fixed subring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain $\mathcal O$ with irreducible element $\pi$, complete for the $\pi$-adic topology, with $\#(\mathcal O/\pi)=r$ and $(r)=(\pi)$, and let $K_0$ be a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Let $Onr$ be a characteristic-zero $\mathcal O$-algebra domain with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $Fr$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, such that every element of $Onr$ satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial over $Onr$ of positive degree has a root modulo $\pi$, and $Fr(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod\pi$ for all $x$. Let $v\!\det:GL_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) be a homomorphism, $G$ a group, $\sigma:G\to GL_2(K_0)$ a homomorphism and $\Gamma\le G$ a subgroup containing an element $z$ with $\sigma z$ a scalar matrix $c\cdot 1$ and $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$. Let $t:T\to\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ be a scheme over $\mathcal O$, and write $\widehat T(B)=\{\varphi:\operatorname{Spec}B\to T\ \text{over}\ \mathcal O\}$ for the functor `Scheme.nilpPoints t` on $\mathcal O$-algebras $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent. Assume given, for each such $B$, a map $\rho'_B$ from pairs $(\psi,P)$ with $\psi:Onr\to_{\mathcal O}B$ and $P$ a Deligne datum over $B$ (an object of `Omega K₀ π`: a $B$-submodule of each base-changed full lattice, with invertible quotient, monotone under inclusions, invariant under homotheties, and nondegenerate at every prime of $B$) to $\widehat T(B)$, natural in $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\varphi:B\to B'$, and invariant in the sense that for $\gamma\in\Gamma$ and $x,x'$ with $x'_1=\mathrm{frobTwist}(Onr,Fr,-v\!\det(\sigma\gamma))(x_1)$ and $x'_2$ the pullback of $x_2$ along $(\sigma\gamma)^{-1}$ one has $\rho'_B(x')=\rho'_B(x)$. Then there exists a family $\rho_2$, defined on pairs consisting of an $\mathcal O$-algebra map to $B$ from the equalizer subalgebra of $Fr\circ Fr$ and the identity of $Onr$ together with a Deligne datum, natural in $B$, satisfying $\rho_2(\psi|_{\text{equalizer}},P)=\rho'(\psi,P)$ for all $\psi:Onr\to_{\mathcal O}B$ and all $P$; and any natural family with this restriction property agrees with $\rho_2$ at every $B$ and every argument.
--
--   This is the descent step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation in which a $\Gamma$-invariant family of points, parametrised by coefficient maps from the completed maximal unramified extension $\widehat{\mathcal O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ together with Deligne data, is shown to factor uniquely through the subring fixed by the square of Frobenius, the central element $z$ with $v\!\det(\sigma z)=2$ providing the required $\mathrm{Fr}^{2}$-equivariance. It is used in the construction of the descended quotient map, `descendedQuotientMap_univ`.
